  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening of Accounting and Auditing Institutional Framework and Practices</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In early 2002, the IRC, in association with the CPCC, made an evaluation of its decade of existence. It identified a huge need for both accounting institutions to a request for Bank assistance, under IDF financing to strengthen accounting and suggested and led a series of activities aimed at implementing accounting standards and practices as well assisting the accounting profession. Due to a lack of cooperation from 1990 - 2001 with international community the request was never processed. This proposed IDF grant would extend resources to strengthen the accounting institutional framework and practices in the DRC. This involves among other things: Component 1: Assessment of the current Institutional Framework and Capacity Component 2: Elaboration of an Institutional Framework Component 3: Establish Resource Center (Information Technology) Objectives of the Grant requested:  This proposed IDF grant would extend resources to strengthen the accounting institutional framework and practices in the DRC.</narrative>
  </description>
